HST Office: a print job waiting on the File panel's Print page ends before its document closes.

The Print page leaves the document usable while its job waits (the print dialog it replaces is modal), so the
document can be closed under the job. Writer then ended its view with the job still open and the office aborted
(Windows: 0xc0000409 / fail-fast): at the end of the Windows session with a changed document on the Print page
(AutoRecovery closes the documents), and on XCloseable.close() from a macro or an extension. Sheets, the window's X
and File > Thoát were not affected. A close guard on the frame and on the document of a job the page takes closes
the panel, which cancels the job, when either is asked to close (queryClosing), before anything closes.

- sfx2/source/backstage/hstbackstage.cxx (PrintPageCloseGuard, lcl_guardPrintPage, lcl_takePrintJob).

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_backstage_print_job_ends_before_close.py; tests/runtime/check-backstage-print-close.py
(Windows: session end, close(True) from a macro, Ctrl+W, the X, .uno:Quit and terminate with the Print page open).

